    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.jump2d\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently mini.jump2d doesn't work well with some Asian languages like Chinese, Japanese, Thai, Khmer,  Tibetan,... because these languages don't like using space and Roman punctuations, so Lua patterns don't work well with them. However, Vim's built-in keyword support can seperate words in these languages better.\n\nUsing Vim's keyword support (via Vim regex `\\k`) also allows users to change the definition of a word just by modifying `'iskeyword'` option, without having to learn some kinds of pattern/regex or override a function.",
